.Dd October 8, 2026
.Dt MANET-CPU-SAMPLE.PY 8
.Os MANET
.Sh NAME
.Nm manet-cpu-sample.py
.Nd measure service CPU use over one interval
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -unit Ar unit
.Op Fl -seconds Ar duration
.Op Fl -label Ar label
.Op Fl h | Fl -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads a service's cgroup-v2 CPU counters before and after a timed interval
and prints JSON.
The sample includes child processes in the service's cgroup.
Output includes service CPU seconds per minute, service usage as a percentage
of one CPU core, and whole-system busy CPU seconds per minute.
Values may exceed one core's capacity when multiple cores are used.
.Pp
The unit must be active with its own cgroup, and its counters must be readable.
A changed service invocation, changed cgroup or reset counter invalidates
the sample; repeat it after the service is stable.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -unit Ar unit
Systemd unit to sample; default
.Li manet-atak.service .
.It Fl -seconds Ar duration
Interval in seconds; default 60, range 1 through 3600.
Fractional values are accepted.
.It Fl -label Ar label
Label included in the JSON output; default
.Li sample .
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print help and exit.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /sys/fs/cgroup/
Service CPU counters from its cgroup's
.Pa cpu.stat .
.It Pa /proc/stat
Aggregate system CPU counters.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
Exits 0 after a valid sample, 1 for an operating error or invalidated sample,
and 2 for invalid arguments.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
manet-cpu-sample.py --unit mesh-status.service --seconds 60
.Ed
